{
  "case_id": "2021-21-418",
  "document_hash": "53dc3c56a3c6a70ddb15f2c727a2973a9e6567fd1880a62bda890046e30032a0",
  "records": [
    {
      "attribution": "Syllabus",
      "case_id": "2021-21-418",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "53dc3c56a3c6a70ddb15f2c727a2973a9e6567fd1880a62bda890046e30032a0",
      "evidence_id": "ev-53dc3c56a3c6-0000-0000",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 2,
        "start": 2
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Petitioner Joseph Kennedy lost his job as a high school football coach in the Bremerton School District after he knelt at midfeld after games to offer a quiet personal prayer."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioner Joseph Kennedy",
      "case_id": "2021-21-418",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "53dc3c56a3c6a70ddb15f2c727a2973a9e6567fd1880a62bda890046e30032a0",
      "evidence_id": "ev-53dc3c56a3c6-0000-0001",
      "kind": "allegation",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 2,
        "start": 2
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Mr. Kennedy sued in federal court, alleging that the District's actions violated the First Amendment's Free Speech and Free Exercise Clauses."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Goldberg",
      "case_id": "2021-21-418",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "53dc3c56a3c6a70ddb15f2c727a2973a9e6567fd1880a62bda890046e30032a0",
      "evidence_id": "ev-53dc3c56a3c6-0000-0005",
      "kind": "concurrence",
      "opinion_part": "concurrence",
      "pages": {
        "end": 6,
        "start": 6
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "School Dist. of Abington Township v. Schempp, 374 U. S. 203, 308 (Goldberg, J., concurring). A government entity's concerns about phantom constitutional violations do not justify actual violations of an individual's First Amendment rights."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2021-21-418",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "53dc3c56a3c6a70ddb15f2c727a2973a9e6567fd1880a62bda890046e30032a0",
      "evidence_id": "ev-53dc3c56a3c6-0001-0000",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": "majority",
      "pages": {
        "end": 10,
        "start": 10
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Mr. Kennedy offered his prayers after the players and coaches had shaken hands, by taking a knee at the 50-yard line and praying \u201cquiet[ly]\u201d for \u201capproximately 30 seconds.\u201d Id., at 168\u2013169."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2021-21-418",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "53dc3c56a3c6a70ddb15f2c727a2973a9e6567fd1880a62bda890046e30032a0",
      "evidence_id": "ev-53dc3c56a3c6-0001-0001",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": "majority",
      "pages": {
        "end": 11,
        "start": 11
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The District explained that it sought to establish \u201cclear parameters\u201d \u201cgoing forward.\u201d Ibid. It instructed Mr. Kennedy to avoid any motivational \u201ctalks with students\u201d that \u201cinclude[d] religious expression, including prayer,\u201d and to avoid \u201csuggest[ing], encourag[ing] (or discourag[ing]), or supervis[ing]\u201d any prayers of students, which students remained free to \u201cengage in.\u201d Id., at 44."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2021-21-418",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "53dc3c56a3c6a70ddb15f2c727a2973a9e6567fd1880a62bda890046e30032a0",
      "evidence_id": "ev-53dc3c56a3c6-0001-0002",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": "majority",
      "pages": {
        "end": 12,
        "start": 12
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "On October 14, through counsel, Mr. Kennedy sent a letter to school officials informing them that, because of his \u201csincerely-held religious beliefs,\u201d he felt \u201ccompelled\u201d to offer a \u201cpost-game personal prayer\u201d of thanks at midfeld. Id., at 62\u201363, 172."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2021-21-418",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "53dc3c56a3c6a70ddb15f2c727a2973a9e6567fd1880a62bda890046e30032a0",
      "evidence_id": "ev-53dc3c56a3c6-0001-0004",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": "majority",
      "pages": {
        "end": 15,
        "start": 15
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "In an October 28 Q&A document provided to the public, the District admitted that it possessed \u201cno evidence that students have been directly coerced to pray with Kennedy.\u201d Id., at 105."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2021-21-418",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "53dc3c56a3c6a70ddb15f2c727a2973a9e6567fd1880a62bda890046e30032a0",
      "evidence_id": "ev-53dc3c56a3c6-0001-0005",
      "kind": "holding",
      "opinion_part": "majority",
      "pages": {
        "end": 16,
        "start": 16
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The District Court denied that motion, concluding that a \u201creasonable observer . . . would have seen him as . . . leading an orchestrated session of faith.\u201d App. to Pet. for Cert. 303."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2021-21-418",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "53dc3c56a3c6a70ddb15f2c727a2973a9e6567fd1880a62bda890046e30032a0",
      "evidence_id": "ev-53dc3c56a3c6-0001-0008",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": "majority",
      "pages": {
        "end": 19,
        "start": 19
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "We begin by examining whether Mr. Kennedy has discharged his burdens, frst under the Free Exercise Clause, then under the Free Speech Clause."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Gorsuch",
      "case_id": "2021-21-418",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "53dc3c56a3c6a70ddb15f2c727a2973a9e6567fd1880a62bda890046e30032a0",
      "evidence_id": "ev-53dc3c56a3c6-0002-0000",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": "majority",
      "pages": {
        "end": 20,
        "start": 20
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "That Mr. Kennedy has discharged his burdens is effec- tively undisputed. No one questions that he seeks to en- gage in a sincerely motivated religious exercise."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Bremerton School District",
      "case_id": "2021-21-418",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "53dc3c56a3c6a70ddb15f2c727a2973a9e6567fd1880a62bda890046e30032a0",
      "evidence_id": "ev-53dc3c56a3c6-0002-0002",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": "majority",
      "pages": {
        "end": 21,
        "start": 21
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "As it put it in its September 17 letter, the District prohibited \u201cany overt ac- tions on Mr. Kennedy's part, appearing to a reasonable ob- server to endorse even voluntary, student-initiated prayer.\u201d"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Gorsuch",
      "case_id": "2021-21-418",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "53dc3c56a3c6a70ddb15f2c727a2973a9e6567fd1880a62bda890046e30032a0",
      "evidence_id": "ev-53dc3c56a3c6-0002-0004",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": "majority",
      "pages": {
        "end": 21,
        "start": 21
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "In this case, the District's challenged policies were neither neutral nor generally applicable."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2021-21-418",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "53dc3c56a3c6a70ddb15f2c727a2973a9e6567fd1880a62bda890046e30032a0",
      "evidence_id": "ev-53dc3c56a3c6-0002-0001",
      "kind": "holding",
      "opinion_part": "majority",
      "pages": {
        "end": 24,
        "start": 24
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Applying these lessons here, it seems clear to us that Mr. Kennedy has demonstrated that his speech was private speech, not government speech."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2021-21-418",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "53dc3c56a3c6a70ddb15f2c727a2973a9e6567fd1880a62bda890046e30032a0",
      "evidence_id": "ev-53dc3c56a3c6-0002-0003",
      "kind": "holding",
      "opinion_part": "majority",
      "pages": {
        "end": 27,
        "start": 27
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The District cannot sustain its burden under any of them."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2021-21-418",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "53dc3c56a3c6a70ddb15f2c727a2973a9e6567fd1880a62bda890046e30032a0",
      "evidence_id": "ev-53dc3c56a3c6-0003-0000",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": "majority",
      "pages": {
        "end": 32,
        "start": 32
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Court has long held that government may not, consistent with a historically sensitive understanding of the Establishment Clause, \u201cmake a religious observance compulsory.\u201d Zorach v. Clauson, 343 U. S. 306, 314 (1952). Government \u201cmay not coerce anyone to attend church,\u201d ibid., nor may it force citizens to engage in \u201ca formal religious exercise,\u201d Lee v. Weisman, 505 U. S. 577, 589 (1992)."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Thomas",
      "case_id": "2021-21-418",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "53dc3c56a3c6a70ddb15f2c727a2973a9e6567fd1880a62bda890046e30032a0",
      "evidence_id": "ev-53dc3c56a3c6-0003-0003",
      "kind": "concurrence",
      "opinion_part": "concurrence",
      "pages": {
        "end": 39,
        "start": 39
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Mr. Kennedy is entitled to summary judgment on his First Amendment claims. The judgment of the Court of Appeals is Reversed.\nJustice Thomas, concurring.\nI join the Court's opinion because it correctly holds that Bremerton School District violated Joseph Kennedy's First Amendment rights."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2021-21-418",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "53dc3c56a3c6a70ddb15f2c727a2973a9e6567fd1880a62bda890046e30032a0",
      "evidence_id": "ev-53dc3c56a3c6-0004-0001",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": "dissent",
      "pages": {
        "end": 41,
        "start": 41
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The Court now charts a different path, yet again paying almost exclusive attention to the Free Exercise Clause's protection for individual religious exercise while giving short shrift to the Establishment Clause's prohibition on state establishment of religion."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2021-21-418",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "53dc3c56a3c6a70ddb15f2c727a2973a9e6567fd1880a62bda890046e30032a0",
      "evidence_id": "ev-53dc3c56a3c6-0005-0000",
      "kind": "dissent",
      "opinion_part": "dissent",
      "pages": {
        "end": 52,
        "start": 52
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The court rejected Kennedy's free exercise claim, fnding the District's directive narrowly tailored to its Establishment Clause concerns and citing Kennedy's refusal to cooperate in fnding an accommodation that would be acceptable to him."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2021-21-418",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "53dc3c56a3c6a70ddb15f2c727a2973a9e6567fd1880a62bda890046e30032a0",
      "evidence_id": "ev-53dc3c56a3c6-0005-0002",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": "dissent",
      "pages": {
        "end": 53,
        "start": 53
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The Court of Appeals denied rehearing en banc, and this Court granted certiorari."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2021-21-418",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "53dc3c56a3c6a70ddb15f2c727a2973a9e6567fd1880a62bda890046e30032a0",
      "evidence_id": "ev-53dc3c56a3c6-0006-0000",
      "kind": "dissent",
      "opinion_part": "dissent",
      "pages": {
        "end": 62,
        "start": 62
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "practice did not violate the Establishment Clause. This decision rests on an erroneous understanding of the Religion Clauses."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2021-21-418",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "53dc3c56a3c6a70ddb15f2c727a2973a9e6567fd1880a62bda890046e30032a0",
      "evidence_id": "ev-53dc3c56a3c6-0006-0001",
      "kind": "dissent",
      "opinion_part": "dissent",
      "pages": {
        "end": 63,
        "start": 63
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Second, the Court contends that the lower courts erred by introducing a false tension between the Free Exercise and Establishment Clauses."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2021-21-418",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "53dc3c56a3c6a70ddb15f2c727a2973a9e6567fd1880a62bda890046e30032a0",
      "evidence_id": "ev-53dc3c56a3c6-0006-0002",
      "kind": "dissent",
      "opinion_part": "dissent",
      "pages": {
        "end": 66,
        "start": 66
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Despite all of this authority, the Court claims that it \u201clong ago abandoned\u201d both the \u201cendorsement test\u201d and this Court's decision in Lemon, 403 U. S. 602."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2021-21-418",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "53dc3c56a3c6a70ddb15f2c727a2973a9e6567fd1880a62bda890046e30032a0",
      "evidence_id": "ev-53dc3c56a3c6-0006-0003",
      "kind": "dissent",
      "opinion_part": "dissent",
      "pages": {
        "end": 67,
        "start": 67
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The Court now goes much further, overruling Lemon entirely and in all contexts."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2021-21-418",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "53dc3c56a3c6a70ddb15f2c727a2973a9e6567fd1880a62bda890046e30032a0",
      "evidence_id": "ev-53dc3c56a3c6-0006-0005",
      "kind": "dissent",
      "opinion_part": "dissent",
      "pages": {
        "end": 70,
        "start": 70
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The Court also distinguishes Santa Fe because Kennedy's prayers \u201cwere not publicly broadcast or recited to a captive audience.\u201d"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2021-21-418",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "53dc3c56a3c6a70ddb15f2c727a2973a9e6567fd1880a62bda890046e30032a0",
      "evidence_id": "ev-53dc3c56a3c6-0007-0000",
      "kind": "dissent",
      "opinion_part": "dissent",
      "pages": {
        "end": 72,
        "start": 72
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The question before the Court is not whether a coach taking a knee to pray on the feld would constitute an Establishment Clause violation in any and all circumstances."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2021-21-418",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "53dc3c56a3c6a70ddb15f2c727a2973a9e6567fd1880a62bda890046e30032a0",
      "evidence_id": "ev-53dc3c56a3c6-0007-0002",
      "kind": "dissent",
      "opinion_part": "dissent",
      "pages": {
        "end": 74,
        "start": 74
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "society's interest in protecting the separation between church and state, eroding the protections for religious liberty for all."
    }
  ],
  "schema_version": "1.0.0"
}
